---
title: Form field
order: 7
description: Labelled inputs and text areas with hint, error and disabled states.
---
{% from "docs.njk" import example, usage, props %}
{% from "components/form-field/form-field.njk" import formField %}
<header class="docs-header">
  <p class="docs-eyebrow">Component · Partial</p>
  <h1>Form field</h1>
  <p class="docs-lede">A label, an optional hint, the control, and a slot for an error message. They're wired together with <code>aria-describedby</code>, so screen readers read the hint and the error with the field.</p>
</header>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="use">
  <h2 id="use">Use it</h2>
  {% set code %}{% raw %}{% from "components/form-field/form-field.njk" import formField %}
{{ formField({ id: "name", label: "Your name", autocomplete: "name", required: true }) }}
{{ formField({ id: "message", label: "What are you after?", multiline: true, hint: "Size, colours, a deadline. Anything helps." }) }}{% endraw %}{% endset %}
  {{ usage(code) }}
  {{ props([
    ["id", "string", "Required. Also used as the name unless you pass name."],
    ["label", "string", "Always required, even when hidden. Use hideLabel only when the purpose is obvious from what's around it."],
    ["type", "string", "Input type. Defaults to text."],
    ["hint", "string", "Help shown under the label."],
    ["error", "string", "Shows the error and sets aria-invalid."],
    ["multiline / rows", "boolean / number", "A textarea instead of an input."],
    ["required / optional", "boolean", "Mark the rare optional field with “(optional)” instead of starring the required ones."],
    ["autocomplete, placeholder, value, disabled", "", "Passed through."]
  ]) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="states">
  <h2 id="states">States</h2>
  <div class="docs-examples">
    {% set ex %}<div class="docs-stack">{{ formField({ id: "ex-name", label: "Your name", autocomplete: "name" }) }}</div>{% endset %}
    {{ example("Default", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}<div class="docs-stack">{{ formField({ id: "ex-size", label: "Rough size", hint: "In centimetres, or describe the wall it's for.", optional: true }) }}</div>{% endset %}
    {{ example("Hint and optional", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}<div class="docs-stack">{{ formField({ id: "ex-email", label: "Email address", type: "email", value: "cali@", error: "That doesn’t look like a valid email address." }) }}</div>{% endset %}
    {{ example("Error", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}<div class="docs-stack">{{ formField({ id: "ex-msg", label: "What are you after?", multiline: true, rows: 4 }) }}</div>{% endset %}
    {{ example("Text area", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}<div class="docs-stack">{{ formField({ id: "ex-dis", label: "Order number", value: "#1042", disabled: true }) }}</div>{% endset %}
    {{ example("Disabled", ex) }}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="copy">
  <h2 id="copy">Error copy</h2>
  <ul class="docs-list">
    <li>Say what to do, in Cali's voice: “Enter your email address to sign up.”, not “Email is required”.</li>
    <li>When a form fails to send: “Something went wrong. Please try again.”</li>
  </ul>
</section>
